# Preserve every committed file byte-for-byte.  `-text` disables all newline
# translation, in both directions, on every platform.
#
# Why this is not cosmetic: `scripts/127_make_docx.py` records the SHA-1 of
# `docs/MANUSCRIPT.md` **as bytes** (`sha1_file` -> `read_bytes`) in the build
# manifest, and `--check` compares that recorded value against the file on disk.
# With the default `core.autocrlf=true` the working tree is rewritten to CRLF on
# Windows and to LF elsewhere, so a clone on another platform computes a
# different hash and reports a **false** "the .docx is stale".  Same for
# `figures_sha1` (taken over `results/figs/FIGURES.json`).
#
# For a repository whose selling point is that its own checks can be trusted, a
# cross-platform false alarm is the worst possible failure: it announces an
# inconsistency that does not exist.  Measured before this file was added:
# MANUSCRIPT.md hashed to af7190eb... (CRLF bytes) while the manifest's recorded
# value matched the CRLF reading only because the working tree was on Windows.
* -text
